<!--
  LAUNCHER ICON — API 24-25 fallback.

  Adaptive icons only exist from API 26, and mipmap-anydpi-v26 shadows this file from
  there on. On 24 and 25 the launcher gets this instead: the full mark with our own
  corner radius already applied, because nothing is going to mask it for us.

  It is a vector, not a set of PNGs. VectorDrawable has been in the framework since
  API 21, so every device that can reach this file can render it, and we avoid
  checking five bitmap densities into the repo for two OS versions.
-->
<inset xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:drawable="@drawable/ic_logo"
    android:inset="0dp"/>
